<p local-id=3D"3ceb0421-85d0-4a98-a4c5-566be6d11d22"></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Storage=
 Efficiency Table
Method=09Original Size=09Final Size=09Space Savings=09Compression Ratio
gson.toJson() [Baseline]=0918,040 bytes=0912,954 bytes=095,086 bytes (28.2%=
)=090.718
getTransientPayload() [Field Removal]=0918,040 bytes=097,009 bytes=0911,031=
 bytes (61.1%)=090.389
getOptimalCompressedTransientPayload() [TypeAdapter]=0918,040 bytes=095,118=
 bytes=0912,922 bytes (71.6%)=090.284</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"ac2d9d37-e4f0-4f97-8969-38fe063ef4ef"></p>
<p local-id=3D"ace9d237-9397-463f-aa55-8c3ad4a35910">=F0=9F=8E=AF Key Findi=
ngs &amp; Recommendations<br>
=F0=9F=8F=86 Winners by Category:<br>
Fastest Performance: getTransientPayload() - 44,553 ops/sec<br>
Best Compression: getOptimalCompressedTransientPayload() - 71.6% space savi=
ngs<br>
Best Balance: getTransientPayload() - Good compression with excellent perfo=
rmance<br>
=F0=9F=93=88 Analysis:<br>
getTransientPayload() is the clear winner for high-throughput scenarios, be=
ing 54% faster than the baseline<br>
getOptimalCompressedTransientPayload() provides the best storage efficiency=
 but at 3.7x slower performance<br>
The compression methods show diminishing returns - they provide additional =
storage savings but with significant performance costs<br>
=E2=9C=85 Final Recommendation:<br>
Use getTransientPayload() for high-throughput, low-latency applications as =
it provides:</p>
<p local-id=3D"a4eec433-24c1-41b9-868a-826e745a7b2d">Fastest processing (22=
.45 =CE=BCs average)<br>
Excellent space savings (61.1% reduction)<br>
No decompression overhead<br>
Best performance/storage balance<br>
The test used real transaction data (18,040 bytes) and performed 5,000 iter=
ations per method with proper warmup cycles, making these results highly re=
liable for production decision-making.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c72ca878-7b24-41e2-806c-077935a0f1d9"></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"926917bd-8415-46a2-97a6-316918de3ffa" id=3D"OptimisingStora=
geforAxonTransactionDatabasewithDBPartitioningandEncodingTechniques-OtherOp=
timisations">Other Optimisations</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c2a21947-13cf-4136-ba5a-6f8707aa23c3">
<li local-id=3D"4ce02515-3133-42e4-a2d7-a24ff7e8b568">
<p local-id=3D"2d41a1e4-9e1f-41bb-824d-d2cec78665a3">Removed castor call de=
pendency in transaction webhooks, at present we are making 2 calls one befo=
re pushing data to topic and other after fetching from topic to get bin rel=
ated information, now with current change ats will call only castor once, a=
s network delay between castor getCard Api with and without these details v=
ery minimal as most of the data is already cached at castor.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1be0f380-3ee6-4396-83e4-e97206fb05bb">
<p local-id=3D"39d65c43-5d09-43f4-a12c-396f4f462a2e">Moving Delta Fetch by =
using eager loading techinque.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"21347193-20d0-4910-82bd-b71cc733fbe2">
<p local-id=3D"555c280e-f477-4c66-ace5-18e16382fb10">Update in select query=
 to remove original message from general matching. query and use this origi=
nal message query only when required, there in bandwidth provided rds can b=
e used to efficiently.</p></li>
</ol>
<h4 local-id=3D"cbff8166-deff-48f4-8a87-a5ba55586f0f" id=3D"OptimisingStora=
geforAxonTransactionDatabasewithDBPartitioningandEncodingTechniques-(ATSOpt=
imisationbymovingdeclinedTransactions)">( ATS Optimisation by moving declin=
ed Transactions)</h4>
<ol start=3D"4" local-id=3D"f948cd96-1a87-4a03-bcf5-ee0bba06d7c7">
<li local-id=3D"d8cdc315-41b2-4287-a579-6e00c2409574">
<p local-id=3D"71ebd5b0-966f-4266-a549-89dd9ba87490">At present we are reta=
ining OTC/OTM records for 3 months it just because of this declined message=
s in these tables or else 2months records would suffice the requirement.</p=
>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"8d4ae43b-776b-4a50-9740-d483638eea87">
<li local-id=3D"478ad3b3-dd9d-4d7f-a93d-4a7370248a03">
<p local-id=3D"c3aa867a-e24b-4c94-8b5a-8aa807e5b8c0">Details: At present if=
 Auth message is declined there is possibility that we may or may not recei=
ve advice message for it. Any declined message is kind of settled transacti=
on there won=E2=80=99t be settlement for these messages. As these are final=
 transactions and we move declined to TC/TM in certain scenarios only we ar=
e retaining OTC/OTM tables for to return that unmoved declined transactions=
 in support center.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"529b9feb-2832-4a3b-954b-9792aa6620c2">
<p local-id=3D"6627b3ad-fd5f-43fc-a1ae-9f30699192cb">Following are differen=
t scenarios which exists in live today</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"195d1459-9c2d-47af-b0d4-cf9aac9a7726">
<li local-id=3D"4e7e2be8-90b8-4c4f-b117-d369055cd4e6">
<p local-id=3D"c76a6f19-d831-4e50-80ec-b1371b120641">0100 (declined)-&gt; R=
ecords will be in OTC/OTM only</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"21d5244c-a943-41c4-a7f2-59a33bf459f4">
<p local-id=3D"bfdb1250-218f-4217-bbcb-f11176a911ad">0100 (declined)-0120(d=
eclined) =E2=86=92 Records will be moved to TC/TM</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"47167130-46c4-4913-8430-ba7d3a6dbfd1">
<p local-id=3D"b1a0687c-e97d-4a34-ac9f-b0e078f6f699">0100(approved)-0120(de=
clined) =E2=86=92 Records will be moved to TC/TM</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4c7aeea6-92db-4dff-a88e-a6105112e763">
<p local-id=3D"18f426bc-05c9-4d1e-9e09-3162a17ab22d">0120 (declined) =E2=86=
=92 Record will be in OTC/OTM only</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c963b5cf-3944-4826-857e-4ee79f54e951">
<p local-id=3D"1f7a5287-5108-4d0b-a6bc-6f16eaf90922">0200 (declined)-&gt; R=
ecords will be OTC/OTM only</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li local-id=3D"f3362ab5-d0ae-42b4-9998-a5213004e9f7">
<p local-id=3D"a11e6162-ffd4-4151-a6bf-37d46b435a2d">With current change ju=
st like on release day we are going to move all declines which are in OTC/O=
TM tables to TC/TM tables after 7 days, as a result we don=E2=80=99t need t=
o maintain OTC/OTM 3 partitions instead 2 will be enough</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2a3216e1-7708-4118-b042-062bd33b4934">
<p local-id=3D"20d6d361-bd9f-41f4-b621-f765cee67aff">Result of this change =
reduce in DB size atleast 800GB (OTC contributes 700+GB per-month with all =
relations + OTM contributes 120GB+)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d5eda8f5-5b9e-4bdb-86c0-e7d4e9fe6fa5">
<p local-id=3D"bf1b932f-7fd7-4c75-bd0b-4ac3efa5a18e">This job runs alongs w=
ith release job hrs with separate endpoint.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">curl --=
location 'https://axon.internal.ohio1-axonstage.zetaapps.in/axon-transactio=
n-service-webhooks/v1/webhooks/tenants/4/transactions/declined/move' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
--header 'X-B3-Sampled: 1' \
--data '{
    "network": "BCFS",
    "batchSize": 10,
    "thresholdInDays": 7
}'</pre>
</div>
</div>
